The bare loop produced useful evidence before the API quota stopped it: two vendors failed `easy`, Gemini solved it, and Terra failed the first `medium` instance. The remaining calls were rejected with OpenRouter’s “total key limit exceeded,” so the harness correctly refused to make a hardness claim. I will not fabricate or reinterpret those errors as failures. I’m using the completed replies to inspect why `easy` was solvable and will harden the construction locally while preserving the witness caps.
